From 2c2ff836aae5a3d7144252754b031f63b7d3b780 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhaowTao <zhaowtao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:01:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Shader prefetch: a launcher setting, and a profile key that
 turns it off (Persona 5 Royal)

A program's shader libraries are loaded in the background as soon as the game makes the
program (nvn_mtl.m mtl_prog_prefetch, from nvnProgramSetShaders), whether or not a draw
uses them. It had a switch, DM_NVN_PREFETCH=0, but no front end could offer it:
dm/ios/Sources/player_env.h filters the DM_NVN_ prefix as a diagnostic, so it cannot be
saved from Documents/env.txt either.

On iOS a loaded library is a mapping the process keeps for good: NvShader holds the
MTLFunction, the function holds the library, and the shader table keeps the shader by
key. A game with a very large shader tree fills the process's mapping limit that way and
is ended with vnode-limit. Persona 5 Royal is 24,826 pipelines, 88,792 metallib and
30,646 json (119,439 files, 1.3 GB) and was ended after 60-100 s in every configuration
tried on an iPhone 17 Pro, while Breath of the Wild (4,829 pipelines) and Rhythm Heaven
Groove (100 metallib) run for hours on the same device and build
(LNPANDY/NX2Apple#665, #666).

Off, one run held 30 fps for 99,600 frames (about 55 minutes) with the switch in
Documents/env.txt, the path a player takes: no jetsam, no vnode-limit, no argument buffer
abort. 34 minutes / 61,200 presents was the same switch set as a launch environment; with
it on the same build aborted in a prefetch worker at 5 min 33 s.

- settings.tsv gains the row for every NVN game, in Performance, with the iOS default
  from the profile and the Mac default on (the shape DM_PSO_MTL4 has).
- player_env.h carries the exception DM_NVN_ENC_THREAD already has, so a player build
  keeps the launcher's value.
- game.py takes the profile key nvn_prefetch (on / off) and writes DM_GAME_NVN_PREFETCH,
  which settings.py resolves as the iOS default.
- Persona 5 Royal's profile sets it off, so a player never has to find the row.
- docs_patches.py classifies the new key (`game` to `host`, memory), or it exits on a
  switch it cannot classify and `tools/engine.py sync` fails once the patches apply. The
  generated docs/agents/game-patches.md is left alone: on this pin the generator's own
  profile-switch table is down to one row (game.py's header_one split left `switches()`
  reading the four lines of header()), so a hand-edit would fight the next regeneration.
- The test covers the row's graphics API, both platforms' defaults and the Mac.

The tests pass (17 in test_launcher_settings.py). Off bounds nothing by itself: the
mappings still grow, from what is drawn instead of what is in the program, and a long
session still ends somewhere.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1209
Reason: Persona 5 Royal fills the iOS mapping limit and is ended after 60-100 s; the prefetch switch existed but no front end could reach it, and the game ships it off in its profile
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#665
